# A ROOT-LEVEL include of a DATA file contributed nothing in the Go
# port: TypeScript merged the JSON's keys into the holding map and Go
# answered as if the line were not there. A KEYED include
# (`y: @"./d.json"`) and a root `.aontu` include were both correct, which
# is why only keyed rows existed in the shared suite. Run, from a
# directory holding d.json as {"j":1}:
#   aontu --trust root:. root-data-include-dropped.aontu
# expected: {"j":1,"x":1}
# actual:   {"x":1}          (Go, before the fix)
# FIXED 2026-09-11: test/spec/file.tsv load-root-*. A data file whose
# value is not a map is now refused at the root in both ports too.
@"./d.json"

x: 1
